# The agents' door to the Toolbox (service `edge`, host port 5556).
#
# A Toolbox toolset is only a boundary when the client cannot reach the
# Toolbox's other endpoints: its own /mcp lists EVERY tool (also
# dev_duckdb_execute_sql), and /api/tool/<name>/invoke and /ui call any tool
# by name, whatever toolset the client was given. So agents get a toolset's
# MCP endpoint and nothing else; analytics_dev is not offered at all.
# The Toolbox itself stays on 127.0.0.1:5555 for a person (README, notebook).
{
	admin off
}

:80 {
	@toolset path_regexp ^/mcp/(analytics_readonly|analytics_metadata|inventory_readonly|cross_catalog|analytics_cube_backed|ontology|analytics_engineered)/?$
	handle @toolset {
		reverse_proxy toolbox:5000 {
			flush_interval -1
		}
	}
	handle {
		respond "not offered to agents: use /mcp/<toolset> (every toolset but analytics_dev)" 404
	}
}
